english:
The signs of the day of judgment is a translation of Ashrat as-Sa’ah(عشرةالساعۃ) or Alamat es-Sa’ah(علامات الساعۃ). Alamat es-Sa’ah(علامات الساعۃ) means; the signs of the Day of Judgment. And these are indications, or milestones in our path towards the day of judgment. The Day of Judgment itself, or As-Sa’ah(الساعۃ); Sa’ah(ساعۃ) means the hour. That's the literal translation of it, but it means the beginning of the day of judgment. That’s As-Sa’ah(الساعۃ). No one knows it, but Allahسبحانه تعالى. Not the Ambiyaa(أنبِيَاء), no one knows it, the angels; This is ‘Ilm al-ghayb(علم الغيب). Only Allah سبحانہ تعالی knows, when the day of judgment is. And that's why, in the Hadith(حديث) of Jibreel (جبرئیل), the famous Hadith(حديث) of Jibreel (جبرئیل), when he came down and he asked Rasool Allah ﷺ;

Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Rasool Allah ﷺ said; The one who is asked, does not know any better than the one who's asking. Jibreel (جبرئیل) was asking Rasool Allah ﷺ; when is the hour? Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

The one who was asked, does not know any better than the one who's asking. Meaning; both of us don’t  know, when the Day of Judgment is. So either Jibreel (جبرئیل) nor Rasool Allah ﷺ knew, when the day of judgment is. It’s in the Ilm(علم) of Allahسبحانه تعالى; it's Ghayb (غیب). But, Rasool Allah ﷺ has told us many of its signs. And there are many signs. And in the area of the signs of the Day of Judgment; there are many strong Ahadith(احاديث), and there are many weak. It's one of the areas where you have to sift through the big load of books and Ahadith(احاديث) to extract the authentic, and it's a very Laborous and difficult job, but Alhamdulillah(ألحمدلله)! There was a book that is written; there's a few books. There's a book by Ibn Kathir(إبن كثير), where he listed the signs of the Day of Judgment. And there's other scholars who have written on this topic. But I think it's a master degree; dissertation or a PhD, Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ)! That was done on this topic of the signs of the Day of Judgment; the authentic Ahadith(احاديث) of the signs of the Day of Judgment; As-Sahih(الصّحيح) name Ashrat as-Sa’ah(عشراط الساعۃ) or Sahih(صحيح) in Alamat es-Sa’ah(علامات الساعۃ). The authentic Ahadith(احاديث) in the signs of the Day of Judgment. It was done by a scholar named  Yusuf Al-Wabil(يوسف الوابل). And that reference, I used it as a primary source for the signs of the day of judgment. And he used the authentic books of Ahadith(احاديث) to list these signs. And he has about more than 50 signs of the Day of Judgment. There are some other books, that have listed almost 100, but you know there might be some weak Ahadith(احاديث) in them. The first sign of the day of judgment. By the way, let me mention a few things before we start talking about the signs themselves. The signs of the Day of Judgment; some of them are actual, or it's an actual event, that can only happen once. And you would have accurate knowledge that it did happen. Like, for example; Rasool Allah ﷺ once said; There will be a fire that will come out of Hijaz(حجاز), and the light of it will reach to a Ash-Sham(ألشَّام), and you will be able to see the next of the camels at night. That's an actual event. And you would know when it happened. And it did happen. But then, there are some other signs of the Day of Judgment, that could happen more than once. Could happen many times. Or you think that it already happened, while it didn't. For example; there's one sign that says, one of the signs of the day of judgment;

There will be a lot of massacre and killing. This is a sign when you see the killing that is happening now in the Ummah(امۃ); we might say that, Wala’hi(والله) maybe this sign already happened. But you never know it might even get worse. There's some signs, where it could happen to a certain extent at one time but, it didn't happen to the full extent. And some of them grow gradually. And there are some signs, which are absolute opposites of each other; like there's one sign that says that, peace was spread and there's another sign that says that, insecurity and conflicts will spread. So these are two different signs; because they're contradicting each other, they can't happen in the same time; they must be happening on a different chronological order. The first sign of the Day of Judgment is the message of Rasool Allah ﷺ;

That's the first sign of the day of judgment . Because, Rasool Allah ﷺsays; Rasool Allah ﷺ says; I was sent as close to the Day of Judgment like, these two fingers are close to each other. Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling us that compared to the lives of humanity on the face of the earth; he is so close to the Day of Judgment, it's like these two fingers together. Rasool Allah ﷺ was saying that, he's in the end of time. It's like, he was in the afternoon of the day, we would examine that the life of human beings on the face of the earth is like a day Rasool Allah ﷺ; his message-hood was at afternoon. It's almost sunset. It's late afternoon. The sun is about to set. And this hadith in Bukhari (بخاری); Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

So that's the first sign. Second sign is, the death of Rasool Allah ﷺ. In this Hadith(حديث) narrated by Al-Bukhari(اَلْبُخَارِيْ); Aouf Ibn Malik(عوف ابن مالك) said that, Rasool Allah ﷺ told me to count six signs before the Day of Judgment; number one my death. That’s  the first of the six signs which Rasool Allah ﷺ mention to Aouf(عوف), and we will talk about the other five. The death of Rasool Allah ﷺ is a sign of the day of judgment. And it was the biggest disaster that afflicted the Muslim ummah(امۃ). In fact there is a Hadith(حديث) Rasool Allah ﷺsays; Whenever you are afflicted with a problem; Then remember your problem in losing me, and your problem will be insignificant. If you ever suffer from a problem, or disaster, or catastrophe that happened in your life; then imagine, that you're not really losing much because the greatest loss is the loss of Rasool Allah ﷺ, and that will make you see your problem as insignificant and small. Anas Ibn Malik رضي الله عنهsays, and this saying of Anas Ibn Malik(انس ابن مالك) is narrated by At-Tirmidhi(ألتِّرمِذِيْ). He says; When Rasool Allah ﷺ came to Madinah(مَدِينَه); Madinah(مَدِينَه) was all light;  light was all over Madinah(مَدِينَه). And when Rasool Allah ﷺ passed away Madinah(مَدِينَه) was dark. And then he said; And as soon as we buried Rasool Allah ﷺ, and the dirt of his grave is still on our hands. We felt that our hearts changed.

And he said, we felt the change in our hearts. So the mere presence of Rasool Allah ﷺ was meant something to them. And by Rasool Allah ﷺ just passing away, as soon as he passed away; they felt that something was missing from Madinah(مَدِينَه).

We didn't recognize our hearts anymore; our hearts were different. Because the; Tumaneenah(طمانينه), and the tranquility in the hearts was felt, when Rasool Allah ﷺ was around. Even if, they are not seeing Rasool Allah ﷺ; even if, he's just in his house. They still felt something by him, just being present with them. And as soon as he left them; they felt that, something was missing. This is the second sign of the Day of Judgment. The third sign is the opening of Jerusalem(یروشلم);

And this sign happened in the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab رضي الله عنه. Abu Ubaidah Amir Bin Jarrah(ابو عبيدة عامر بن الجراح) was leader of the army, and he was surrounding Jerusalem(یروشلم). And Jerusalem(یروشلم) had to surrender; they had no chance of fighting the Muslim army. Therefore they sent a message; telling Abu Ubaidah (ابو عبیدہ) that, we're willing to surrender and hand you over the keys to Jerusalem(یروشلم), but we want to give it to the Khalifah(خليفه) of the Muslims. This town is so important; we have to hand the keys to him. Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) asked the Sahabah(صحابه); he made Shu'raa(شعراء); should I go out or should I stay. Some of the Sahabah(صحابه) said; No you should stay in Madinah(مَدِينَه), don't go out it's dangerous for you. And some of the Sahabah(صحابه) said; go!

Go! And In Sha' Allah(ان شاء الله), it will be safe. Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) went out, and we talked about this story of his before, just briefly. He went with his servant, and they were taking turns on the camel. Umar(عُمَر) would ride for a while, and then the servants would ride for a while, and then; they would give the camel time off. When Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was approaching Jerusalem(یروشلم); it was his turn to pull the camel, and it was the turn of his servant to ride the camel. And they pass next to a pool of mud. And Umar(عُمَر)  had to go through it. So he picked up his clothes, and he cross the mud, and his feet were soaked with mud and his clothes. And he's climbing out of this pool of mud dragging the camel. And this is happening in front of the people in Jerusalem(یروشلم); they're seeing the scene in front of their eyes. Abu Ubaidah Amir Bin Jarrah رضي الله عنه; one of the Ashra Mubashra(عشره مبشره) in Jannah(جنة); he felt that this is not appropriate. Not because, the leader should not be humble. No! But he felt that these people; the Romans, and the people living in that area; they have been living in a certain culture, where they see that the leaders and the keys are surrounded with guards, and they present themselves in a certain way. He felt it might not be appropriate for Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) to come like this, because they might not give him the respect that he deserves. Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) deserves respect more than any other person on earth at that time. So he told Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب); he went to the Ameer Ul-Mo'mineen(أميرالمؤمنين), and gave him a few suggestions. Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) hit him in his chest and said; I wouldn't expect this to come from you, and then he said;

Umar(عُمَر) said; We were people who were humiliated; we were nothing. And Allah honored us with Islam. And if we seek honour any other way; Allah Will humiliate us. Meaning our honor is not based on the entourage and the motorcade and the security guards, and the clothes that we wear, and the guards that surround us and those extravagant scenes. That's not where our honour lies; our honour is in Islam. It's not in the clothes that we wear. Because he was wearing a dress that had 14 patches in it. He is teaching Abu Ubaidah(ابو عبیدہ) lesson, and he say; Forget about what they think. It doesn't matter what they think. Allah Will put our honour in their hearts; even if we don't present ourselves the way that they expect. And then he made it clear to Abu Ubaidah(ابو عبیدہ) that, if we try to honour ourselves with any superficial fashion; Allah Will take away the honour from us. Because our honour is only in Islam; it's not in any other way. We don't have to be superficial and ceremonial. We are a simple people, and Allah Will give us honour through this religion. And Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was right. When the people of Jerusalem(یروشلم) saw him in that fashion; they started crying. And it says that the people were standing on the roofs of their houses, looking at this. Because they hear about the name of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), and they never saw him before. They're expecting to see something, and they saw something else. They saw the simplicity of Islam. They couldn't believe their eyes and they were crying. And they handed Al-Khalifah(الخليفه); Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) the keys of Jerusalem(یروشلم). Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ)! It mentions like in the book of Ibn Kathir(إبن كثير), that they had in their books, the signs of the one who will get the keys. And one of his Signs is that, he will have 14 patches in his clothes, that was mentioned in Ibn Kathir(إبن كثير) that, this is one of the signs. And this sign of Bayt-ul-Maqdis(بيت المقدس) is one of the six, and that Hadith(حديث) as we mentioned, is in Bukhari(بخاريْ). And then, sign number four is;

Rasool Allahﷺ says; A death that will eat you away, like certain illness or disease that afflicts goats. And this is talking about, At-Ta'oon(اطاعون); the plague. And this plague occurred in the 18th year of Hijrah(هجرة). And it happened in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام); after the opening of Jerusalem(یروشلم). It just happened after the opening of Jerusalem(یروشلم) in Ash-Sham(ألشَّام). And it was a major disaster for the Muslims; it was a great loss for the ummah(امۃ). Because more than 25,000 Muslims died in that plague. And among the well known names is; Abu Ubaidah(ابو عبیدہ). Abu Ubaidah(ابو عبیدہ) died in that plague, Muadh Ibn Jabal(معاذاِبن جبل) died in that plague, many of the Sahabah(صحابه) died in that plague. For them; it's the blessing of Allah. Because, Ta’oon(طاعون) is a Shahadah(شَهَادَة). Ta’oon(طاعون) is one form of Shahadah(شَهَادَة); martyrdom. But it was a loss for the ummah(امۃ) to lost 25000, just like that. And this is one of the signs of the Day of Judgment. The fifth sign; the abundance of wealth. Rasool Allahﷺ says;

Rasool Allah ﷺ says that, Wealth will be so abundant. A man would be handed 100 dinar. Dinar is a small weight of gold. 100 dinar and they wouldn't be satisfied. What is this? You given me 100 dinar, it's nothing. There will be so much wealth. This happened to a certain extent in the time of Umar Bin Abdul Aziz(عمر بن عبدالعزيز), also to a limited extent in the time of  Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب). In the time of Umar Bin Abdul Aziz(عمر بن عبدالعزيز); there's a few stories. One of them is that the state of Africa, which was at that time, North Africa was called Afriqia. They sent an amount of money to the Khalifah(خليفه) in Madinah(مَدِينَه). Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said; Why are you sending me this money? Why is the state of Africa, sending me this money? This money is supposed to be taken from the rich and given to the poor of the same area. In other words, the money doesn't go to the central government; doesn't go to the federal government; it goes to the local government; to be spent in the same area. They told Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) that, we didn't find any poor person to give this money to. Yeah, this is Umar Bin Abdul Aziz(عمر بن عبدالعزيز). Umar bin  Abdul aziz(عمر بن عبد العزیز) said; They'll send it back to the state of Africa and use it to pave roads or to free slaves. And also the time of the Umar Bin Abdul Aziz(عمر بن عبدالعزيز), the Zaka'at(زكوة) of Yemen was sent. And the same thing, he said; Send it back. So there was an abundance of wealth, because of the Barakah(بركة). Allahسُبحانه وتعالى put blessing in their Rizq(رزق). But this could also refer to the end of time. And that is when, there would be a truly an abundance of wealth all over the world. Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; A time will come, when a man would go out with Zaka'ah(زكوة), with Sadaqah(صدقة), gold, not paper money, gold; and would not find anyone to accept it. Imagine! Going around with gold; offering it to the people and nobody wants to take it. And this Hadith(حديث) is in Muslim. Because there will be so much abundance of wealth, people will have dignity; they wouldn't want to ask for any money; everybody's satisfied everybody's content. Because; I mean you could find people now who have money, they would be willing to take up a Sadaqah(صدقة) of gold. But this hadith tells us two things. First of all; it tells us that, the people are contented and satisfied; they have enough money. It also tells us that, the people are not greedy. Because, there could be a person who was rich, but they would still take Sadaqah(صدقة), if it is gold. And that time, there is also another Hadith(حديث) in a Muslim that says that the earth;

Rasool Allah ﷺ said; The earth vomit, literally vomit columns of gold and silver, just gold and silver coming out of the earth. And the murderer would come and say; I killed people for this. Meaning in the past; I used to kill people for money. And the one who stole, the thief will say; I used to steal for this. And the one who betrayed his family, and cut his kinship would say; I betrayed and I fought my family for this;

And then nobody will take it. They will say; We used to kill people for this. In the past, we used to kill people for this; we used to steal this; we used to fight our families for this money, and now we're not going to take it. People are content in their heart; they're not taking that anymore; they would leave it. Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ)! It might be also, because they have suffered so much. Because there's another sign of the day of judgment that, the river of Euphrates would uncover a mountain of gold. And then, Rasool Allah ﷺ says; If you see it, leave it alone. Because out of every 100 that go there, 99 will be killed. So much bloodshed occurred over money, that in the end, people will just give up; they will say we don't want this anymore, it's causing us so much suffering and pain, we don't want it anymore. I killed people for that, I stole, I fought my family for that; I don't want it know. Another Hadith(حديث), Rasool Allah ﷺ says; And this is a warning; this Hadith(حديث) is a warning for us, this is in Sahih Al-Muslim(صحيح ألمسلم) Muslim;

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; I was given the keys of the treasures of the earth. I don't worry poverty, but that's not my concern. I'm not concerned that you might be poor. Rasool Allah ﷺ said; My concern is that, you would compete on this world. And that would destroy you. That's would destroy you, if we compete on the material games of this world that will destroy us. And Rasool Allah ﷺ said; I don’t fear a poverty, and whatever poverty we have in the Ummah(امة) now, it's not because of lack of resources. Because the best that the world can offer is in the Muslim world. Whether we're talking about precious metals, or oil or agricultural land, the problem is unfair distribution, oppression, people are not giving up their Zaka'ah(زكوة), people are not  giving out Sadaqah(صدقة), that's the problem. So the poverty that we have, is not due to lack of resources. It is because Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)!if you look at the world today; you would find that the dependency is not that much on resources. It is the human being who is the greatest asset. Take a place like Silicon Valley for example, the Silicon Valley is a valley of dirt of silicon, there's nothing in it. There used to be agriculture before, but not anymore, not that much. And it's the richest place on the face of the earth; there's so much money in that place. There's no oil beneath the surface; there's not so much agriculture in the area; there's no place, there's no gold and silver are beneath the surface. What is there? What is on it? It is human resources. It's the mines. And that is the biggest asset. Unfortunately, in the Muslim world now, we have a lot of resources, but we don't have the ability to make use of it. And Allah سبحانہ تعالی Will not give us Barakah(بركة); blessing in our Rizq(رزق); unless we follow the terms of Shariah(شريعة) in business law. If we are cheating, if there is a;

Then Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Will not give blessing in the Rizq(رزق), even if a person is wealthy; Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Will not make the people benefit out of that wealth. Because a person could have money, but if the money does not have Barakah(بركة), doesn't have the secret elements in it; there's no good in that money. The sixth sign of the Day of Judgment is, times of trials and tribulations; Al-Fitan(فتن). Rasool Allah ﷺ says in the Hadith(حديث) narrated by a Al-Imam Muslim(الاِمَام مُسلِم);

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Do good deeds, before the times of trials and tribulations that are like darkness of the mind. Rasool Allahﷺ is telling; do the good deeds now, because the time will come, when it is so dangerous. The trials and tribulations and problems will be like, pieces of dark night spreading all over. And then Rasool Allah ﷺ says; In those times, a man would be a believer in the morning, by nighttime; he's a disbeliever. Another man would be a believer at nighttime. By the morning, they're disbeliever. Why? Rasool Allahﷺ says;

They're selling their religion for worldly benefit. The person is a believer, they have Eeman(ايمان). But they sold this religion to make some money, to make a worldly gain. They gave it up. In another Hadith(حديث), this is narrated by Al Imam Ahmad(الاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ);

It is the same Hadith(حديث), but the difference over here is that Al-Hassan Al-Basri(ألحسن ألبصري) is giving an explanation to that Hadith(حديث). He says;

Al-Hassan Al-Basri(ألحسن ألبصري) says; In the name of Allah I have seen them; we have seen these people. He says; forms, but no minds; bodies without any conscious, like mass attracted to a fire, and flies attracted by greed; they would go for two Dirhams(درهم), and they would come back for two Dirhams(درهم). A person would be willing to sell their religion, for the price, the small price, the miser price of a goat. And then he said, there are forms; you see bodies, but no minds, no conscious; they're willing to give up their religion for a very small price $2 would send them out, $2 would bring them back. You can attract the person; $2 is enough to bring the person, $2 is enough to send them away. Forms without any mind, without any conscious, willing to sell the religion for the price of Al-Anz(العنز); a goat. Al-Hassan Al-Basri(ألحسن ألبصري) saying this in the time of At-Taba'een(ألتابعين). I wonder what he would have said, if you live today. There's another Hadith(حديث), and this might be talking about a different time. Rasool Allahﷺ says;

Imam Ahmad(اِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ) narrates this Hadith(حديث) is similar to the other one, but it just says in the end. The one who's sitting; is better than the one who's standing, and the one who is standing; is better than the one who's walking, and the one who's walking; is better than the one who's running. So break your bows and stay home. And if anybody enters into your home, then be like the best of the two sons of Adam(آدَم). What does this mean? It means that, it's better to stay away from those trials and tribulations. There will be a time when things will be so obscure, so mixed up, you cannot separate truth from falsehood; everything is mixed. Everything is in the gray area. Rasool Allah ﷺ says; Withdraw! Withdraw! Stay away. And the one who's sitting down, is better than the one who's standing meaning; you are sitting down you are away from it, you're better than the one who is standing. And the one who is standing; is better than one who's walking, and the one who is walking; is better than the one who's running . Meaning, don't involve. Have the least involvement, and stay home. And if somebody comes into your house, don't fight them, and be like the best of the two sons of Adam(آدَم). What does that mean? Qabeel(قابيل) and Habeel(هابيل). Qabeel(قابيل) killed Habeel(هابيل). Habeel(هابيل) said that, if you extend your hand forced to kill me, I'm not going to fight back. And even though, it promotes withdrawing out of the Fitan(فتن), but this is talking about specific times. We should not stay home now, and not do anything, and say that, we following this Hadith(حديث). This is talking about times, when things are obscure, and you cannot tell the difference between truth and falsehood. In terms of Fitan(فتن); there are a lot of Fitan(فتن) that already happened, and there are many Fitan(فتن) that did not happen. Rasool Allah ﷺ pointed to the east and said; the Fitan(فتن) come out from here. He pointed to the direction of the East. He was in Madinah(مَدِينَه), and he is pointing to the direction of the east and said; This is the source of Fitan(فتن). And he said, that's where the horn of Shaytan(شَيْطَانْ)  comes out; evil. We find out that some of the greatest trials and tribulations; the source of them was from the east. We're talking about the east of Madinah(مَدِينَه). That doesn't mean that, all of the Fitan(فتن) come out from that area; but it means that that is a primary area of Fitan(فتن). Because Rasool Allah ﷺ mentioned that, there will be wars between you and the Romans and other areas of the world. That's not the only source of Fitan(فتن). But if we look at some of the biggest trials that have caused the greatest problems for this ummah(امة); we would find that, that's where they started from, from the east. Examples of that, many of the deviant sex came out from the east. Political unrest was mostly coming from the direction of the East. And then At-Tatar(التّتار); the Mongolians. And we know the Fitnah(فِتْنَه), that was caused by At-Tatar(التّتار); the Changaiz Khan(چنگيز خان) and the all of that the Holako and Taimor Lenk, it's all came out from the east. Ad-Dajjal(الدّجّال), Rasool Allah ﷺ says; he comes out from the east. And Yajuj(ياجوج) and Majuj(ماجوج); they also come out from the direction of the east. Some of the Fitan(فتن) that already appeared. Number one, the assassination of Uthman(عثمان). And this was the beginning of the Fitan(فتن). The assassination of Uthman(عثمان) was the first Fitnah(فِتْنَه), and it opened the door. It opened the door of every Fitnah(فِتْنَه) after it. There is a narration by Al-Bukhari(اَلْبُخَارِيْ) of a conversation that happened between Huzaifa(حذیفہ) and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب).  Actually Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) was in a meeting, was in a gathering with many of the Sahabah(صحابه), and he asked them; Who of you can tell me the Hadith(حديث) of the Fitnah(فِتْنَه). So Huzaifa(حذیفہ) said; I will, I can tell you the Hadith(حديث) of the Fitnah(فِتْنَه). And he mentioned to him some Ahadith(احاديث). That isn't what Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) wanted to hear. He was talking about another Fitnah(فِتْنَه). Fitnah(فِتْنَه) means, trial or tribulation. He said; I'm not asking you about this.

He said; I'm asking you about the trial, that will move like the waves of the ocean. I'm asking you about the big Fitan(فتن). That will move like the waves of the ocean. Huzaifa(حذیفہ) said;

Huzaifa(حذیفہ) said; Don't worry about it, because between you and those trials is a closed door. He's telling Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب); you shouldn't worry about that, because there's a door between you and those Fitan(فتن). Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) asked Huzaifa(حذیفہ). He told him;

He said; Well the door be open or broken. Huzaifa(حذیفہ) said; It will be broken. Umar(عُمَر) said; If it's broken, then it will never be locked again. If the door is broken, that means it's going to be broken for good. Look at the specific question .He said; Will it be broken or open? Because if you open the door; you could lock it. But if you break the door that’s it, it's open. The door is open. Huzaifa(حذیفہ) was mentioning this to some of the At-Taba'een(ألتابعين). When Huzaifa(حذیفہ)finished, they asked him; Did Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) know, who the door was? Huzaifa(حذیفہ) said; Yes, he knew. Because I told him who was the door, and then Huzaifa(حذیفہ) left. They sent someone to go and ask Huzaifa(حذیفہ); who was the door? Huzaifa(حذیفہ) said; Umar(عُمَر) was the door. Umar(عُمَر) was a door between Fitan(فتن) and this Ummah(امة). In the time of Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) , there was peace and security, and there was stability. There was no trials in the time of Umar(عُمَر). In the time of Umar(عُمَر); it was expansion, it was stability. After Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) passed away; that's when the problems started. But as long as Umar(عُمَر) was living; it was security in the Muslim Ummah(امة). It was expansion. Things were getting better. After Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب)  passed away; that's when the Fitan(فتن)started. Then Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) became the Khalifah(خليفه). Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was killed, was assassinated. The difference between the assassination of Umar(عُمَر) and Uthman(عثمان) is that, the assassination of Umar(عُمَر) was done by a disbeliever. But the assassination of Uthman(عثمان) was done by people, under the name of Islam. And that's why, it opened the door of disunity. Because over there in the case of Umar(عُمَر), it was an enemy of Islam. Over here, it's Muslims among themselves . Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was the Khalifah(خليفه), and some issues happened during his Khilafah(خِلَافَه). And in the end, some Muslims gathered, then it was a Fitnah(فِتْنَه) and they surrounded his house, and they wanted him to give up Khilafah(خِلَافَه). They were asking him to step down. Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was told by Rasool Allah ﷺ;

Uthman(عثمان) remembers that, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; Allah Will give you a cloak. If the people asked you to take it off, don’t . Uthman(عثمان) had no idea, what this meant. Allah is going to give you a cloak. And then the people are going to ask you to take it off. Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; If they ask you to take it off; don't take it off. He understood what it meant, when the people were asking him to step down from Khilafah(خِلَافَه). This Khilafah(خِلَافَه); Allah Has given it to him, and the people are telling him; to take it away, to give it up. So he refused. But in the same time, Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) refused to fight them. So it was a difficult situation. Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب); he and his sons; they were guarding Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان), and Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) told Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان); Give me your orders, we will find them. Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) said;

I don't want one drop of blood to be shed for my cause. I don't want any killing to happen to safeguard me. And he refused to allow Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)  to fight for him. He told Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب); Don't fight them. Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) told his sons; Al-Hassan(الحسن) wa'Al Hussain(وَاَلحسين) to guard Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان). But Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) said that, he doesn't want anybody to fight for him. Eventually, they came in, these people; they were in 1000s. They were surrounding. They're in Madinah(مَدِينَه), and they were surrounding the house of Al Khalifah(الخليفه), and then in the end, they came in and they killed Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان). They killed the Khalifah(خليفه). And that opened the injury, and cause the Fitan(فتن) after that. And Rasool Allah ﷺ did mentioned that Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) will die as a Shaheed(شَهِيد). Rasool Allah ﷺ was with Abu Bakr(ابوبكر), Umar(عُمَر) and Uthman(عثمان) on the mountain of Uhud(أحَد), so the mountain shook. The mountain was shaking; it was an earthquake. Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

Rasool Allah ﷺ told the mountain; Stay stable. Don't move, because on top of you is a prophet, and a Siddique(صديق) and two Shaheed(شَهِيد), two martyrs in the sake of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى. Rasool Allah ﷺ and Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) and Uthman(عثمان) and Umar(عُمَر). The next Fitnah(فِتْنَه) that happened after that, was the Battle of Al-Jamal(الجمل). When Uthman Ibn Affan(عثمان ابن عفان) was killed; there was no Khalifah(خليفه). Some of the Muslims, they came to Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and they said; We will give you  Baiyah(بَيْعة) of Khilafah(خِلَافَه). Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said; No, don't give me Baiyah(بَيْعة) until, the Muslims make Ash-Shu'rah(الشّورى) and then, they decide. They told Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) that, you know that Uthman(عثمان) was killed, and there is a Fitnah(فِتْنَه), and the killers of Uthman(عثمان) are going to spread all over, and the problems will get bigger. It's going to take a while until, the ummah(امة) make Shu'rah(شورى). Therefore you must be the Khalifah(خليفه). And they insisted Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب). He refused in the beginning; he said, let the Muslim will make Shu'rah(شورى). But they insisted on him, and in the end; he agreed. They told him; We have to have a leader. We have to have somebody to go and bring the Muslims together again. They gave Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) Baiyah(بَيْعة). Az-Zubair(أزبير) and Talha(طلحة) gave Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) Baiyah(بَيْعة) also. What happened is; that the killers of Uthman(عثمان); they infiltrated the army of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب). And they were in hundreds, maybe in thousands. Talha(طلحة) and Az-Zubair(أزبير) and Ayeshaرضي الله عنها; they wanted the killers of Uthman(عثمان) to be brought to justice. And because the killers of Uthman(عثمان) infiltrated the army of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), they went to Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and they told him; We have to set a court, for the ones who killed the Khalifah(خليفه). Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) refused. And he said;

He said; The Awliya(اولياء) Uthman(عثمان) have to come forth, and ask for his revenge. And the Awliya(اولياء) are the closest relatives of the deceased. In the Islamic Shariah(شريعة); if somebody is killed, is murdered; then his closest relatives are the ones who ask for justice. And because, they have the decision of either asking for execution or accepting the financial compensation. Who makes that decision? It's not the court. It's the family of the deceased, Al-Awliya(ال اوليا). Because if somebody was murdered, intentionally, then the murderer is either executed, or the murderer pays Ad-Diya(الدّيه); compensation. Who makes the decision whether is executed or financial compensation? It is the relatives of the deceased. So Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said; I'm waiting for the relatives of the deceased to come forth. Az-Zubair(أزبير) and Talha(طلحة) and Ayesha(عائشه); they agreed with Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب). At that point, things were fine. It was night time. Some of these killers of Uthman(عثمان), who were in  the army of Ali(علي). They attacked at night. They attacked the army of Talha(طلحة), Zubair(زبير) and Ayesha(عائشه). Now, Talha(طلحة) and Zubair(زبير) and Ayesha(عائشه); they did not come out for fighting. They came out in a big army. But they came out to ask for justice. These men, who killed Uthman(عثمان) and were infiltrating the army of Ali(علي); they attacked at night time. Az-Zubair(أزبير) and Talha(طلحة) thought that Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) attacked, and that's how fighting started. And then in the end, it settled. After that, it was a very brief fight. But in the end, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was able to convince them that, he didn’t attack and that, he is right in his opinion, and they agreed. Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) was once told by Rasool Allah ﷺ that, something will happen between you and Ayesha(عائشه);

Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب); Something will happen between you and Ayesha(عائشه). And this is narrated by Al-Imam Ahmad(الاِمَامْ اَحْمَدْ). Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said; “Between me and Ayesha(عائشه)? Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Yes. Ali(علي) said;

He said them; I am the most unfortunate of people. Something happens between me and the mother of the believers Ayesha(عائشه), I must be a very unfortunate person. Rasool Allah ﷺ said; No. And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said; And when that happens; then take her back to safety. Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) went to Ayesha(عائشه), and he is the one, who ordered some of his army soldier to accompany her back to Madinah(مَدِينَه) to safety. This was a fulfillment of the prophecy of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

After the battle of Al Jamal(الجمل); the next Fitnah(فِتْنَه) was Ma'rakat Siffeen(مَعْرَكَة صِفِّينَ); The battle of Siffeen(صِفِّينَ). This was a big Fitnah(فِتْنَه). And Rasool Allah ﷺ was mentions that in a Hadith(حديث) narrated by Al-Bukhari(اَلْبُخَارِيْ) and Muslim(ألمسلم).

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; There will be a war between two big armies of Muslims, and they are fighting for the same cause. Both of them; they want the same thing, but they are still fighting. And this is a contradiction. How could you fight for the same reason? Usually, you would fight for different reasons. Over here, they're fighting for the same cause. They both want the same thing nevertheless, they're still fighting. The interpretation of this is following. As I mentioned to you that, the killers of Uthman(عثمان); the murders of Usman (عثمان) were in the army of Ali(علي), and they were in 1000s. Muawiya(معاويه) was the Wali(ولي) of Uthman(عثمان). Muawiya(معاويه) was the relative of Uthman(عثمان). So he was the one, who has the authority to ask for justice in the case of Uthman(عثمان). It's Muawiya(معاويه). It is Muawiya(معاويه). He is a relative of Uthman(عثمان). He's the Wali(ولي). He has the authority of asking for the murderers of Uthman(عثمان) to be brought to justice. He asked Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) to hand him over. Hand me over to the ones who killed my cousin. Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said; I will. But I need to establish my authority first. These are hundreds, the ones who killed Uthman Ibn Affan رضي الله عنه are hundreds; I cannot just hand them over like that. A big battle; a big Fitnah(فِتْنَه) will happen. You have to give me Baiyah(بَيْعة) first. Everyone in the ummah(امة) has to give me Baiyah(بَيْعة) first that I'm the Khalifah(خليفه). And when I have the authority, given to me by the Muslims, then I will hand them over. But I can't hand them over now, I don't have any authority in my hand. Because you did not give me Baiyah(بَيْعة) yet. Muawiya(معاويه) said; No, I will not give you Baiyah(بَيْعة), until you hand them over. So Muawiya(معاويه) is asking for the blood of Uthman(عثمان), and Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) is willing to take them to justice. But the difference here is that, Muawiya(معاويه) wants Ali(علي) to hand them first; Ali(علي) wants Muawiya(معاويه) to give him the Baiyah(بَيْعة) first. The right side, obviously was Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب). Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) had the right justification. Muawiya(معاويه) made an Ijtihaad(اجتهاد), and it was a wrong Ijtihaad(اجتهاد). He is still the Sahabi(صحابي) of Rasool Allah ﷺ. He is the one Katab Al-Wahi(كتب الوحى). The one who used to write down revelations. He is one of the ones whom Rasool Allah ﷺ entrusted with writing down the Qur'an. And he is the brother-in-law of Rasool Allah ﷺ. Because Rasool Allah ﷺ is married to his sister; Umme Habeebah(أمّ حبيبه). Umme Habeebah(أمّ حبيبه) is the sister of Muawiya(معاويه). Umme Habeebah Binte Abi Sufiyan(أمّ حبيبه بنت ابى سفيان). So he's the brother in law of Rasool Allah ﷺ. But, the right side; the ones who are on the right track; was obviously the army of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب). And there's an indication of that; Rasool Allah ﷺ is Telling Ammar Bin Yasir(عمار بن ياسر);

Rasool Allah ﷺ told Ammar Bin Yasir(عمار بن ياسر); You will be killed by the transgressing side. Ammar Bin Yasir(عمار بن ياسر) was fighting in the army of Ali(علي), and he was killed by the army of Muawiyah(معاويه). He was killed by the transgressing side. But we cannot accused Muawiyah(معاويه), because Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Two groups of Muslims will fight each other. So Rasool Allah ﷺ called both armies; Muslims. The army of Ali(علي), and the army of Muawiya(معاويه); they are both Muslims; fighting each other. And this Hadith(حديث) is in Bukhari (بخاری) and Muslim(مسلم). The next Fitnah(فِتْنَه) was the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of Al-Khawarij (الخوارج). When Ali(علي) and Muawiyah(معاویہ) fought; Ali(علي) army had the upper hand. And the army of Muawiyah (معاویہ) was losing. Muawiyah(معاويه) surrendered. And the way they surrendered is, they put Al-Musahif(المصاحف); Mushaf(مصحف) is the Qur'an; they put it on top of their swords. So they raised up the Musahif(مصاحف); the raised up the Qur'an on their swords. Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب), when he saw that; he quit fighting. They raised the book of Allah سبحانہ تعالی; they surrendered; we're going to stop fighting them. There were people in the army of Ali, who were benefiting from war and bloodshed. They wanted disunity in the Ummah(امة). They didn't want the fighting to stop. They wanted this war to continue; just like they caused this battle between Ali(علي) and Zubair(زبير) and Talha(طلحة). They wanted war to continue with Ali and Muawiyah(معاويه). And these were some of the leaders of some of the tribes, who were benefiting from this bloodshed. And they were the ones who are inflaming this problem. They were exaggerating it, and they were causing it, and they existed on both sides. These are people, who benefiting from bloodshed among Muslims. They said; how can Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) give up. This is the Hukum(حكم) of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى, Ali(علي) is putting the opinion of men over the order of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى. The Hukum(حكم) of Allah; the order of Allah is that, we should fight them, but Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) has given precedence to the opinion of men over the order of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى. And they accused Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) in the beginning, of making a mistake, and then they accused him of Kuffr(كفر). And they accused obviously Muawiyah(معاويه) and Amr Bin Al-Aas(عَمْرُو بِن اَلْعَاص) of Kuffr(كفر) earlier. And they broke out from the army of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and that's where, they got their name Khawarij (خوارج). Khawarij (خوارج) means people who broke off . Khawarij(خوارج) are the ones who broke off. They broke off from the army of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب). Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) Abdullah Ibn Abbas(عبدالله ابن عبّاس) to have a dialogue with them. Abdullah Ibn Abbas(عبدالله ابن عبّاس) succeeded in convincing 4,000 to come back. And this was the beginning of the formation of the sect of Al-Khawarij(الخوارج).  Their lineage; the source of Al-Khawarij(الخوارج) existed in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ. The major characteristic of Al-Khawarij(الخوارج) is extremism. And that existed, with some of the people in the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ. There is a Hadith(حديث) narrated in Bukhari(بخاريْ);

Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(أبو سعید الخدری) says that, when Rasool Allah ﷺ was dividing the booties of war; there's a man from Bani Taneem(بنى تنيم), his named is Zul-Khuwaysarah(ذوالخو یصرۃ). He came to Rasool Allah ﷺ with pride and arrogance, and he's telling Rasool Allah ﷺ; Be just. Look at the rudeness of this man; he is coming to Rasool Allah ﷺ, and he's ordering him to be just.

Be just. Rasool Allah ﷺ said; Woe to you! Who could do justice if I did not? I would be a desperate loser, if I did not do justice. You telling me to be just. The messenger of Allahسُبحانه وتعالى; if I am not just who will be just. Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) said;

Let me chop of his head. Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; Rasool Allah ﷺ told Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب); Leave him alone. He will have followers or descendants,

Companions; whom you would see, your prayer compared to theirs as insignificant. And your fasting compared to theirs as insignificant. Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying; that they would worship Allah so much that the Sahabah(صحابه); their Salah(صلوة) compared to the Salah(صلوة) of these Khawarij(خوارج) will be nothing, and the fasting of the Sahabah(صحابه) would be less than their fasting. From the outside, they seem to be very righteous; they pray so much and they fast so much. Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

They read  Qur'an, but it doesn't go past their throats. In that Qur'an, has no application in their life; it's just words that are coming out from the throat. But in the inside there's no Qur'an. You hear Qur'an; but there is no Qur'an in the mind; there's no Qur'an in the heart. And then Rasool Allah ﷺ said; They would leave religion, like the arrow would leave the target. Sometimes if you shoot a target, if the shot is, the arrow is so strong, and it hits the target with a powerful strength; what will happen is; the arrow would leave the target so fast you wouldn't even notice it. It would so fast, it didn't even pick up any blood. That means that, they would leave the religion so fast and so swift; you wouldn't even notice it. They're so fast and leaving the religion, because of their extreme positions. You see them they're praying; they're fasting; they're doing very well in Ibadah(عبادة). But they have already left their religion a lot of time ago, you didn't even know about it. You will see from the outside a lot of righteousness, but from the inside; it's rigid, and it's like a solid rock. And Rasool Allah ﷺ  was telling Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب) that, the sources of this were people like Al-Khuwaysara(الخو یصرۃ). Al-Khuwaysara(الخو یصرۃ);  did you see the pride and arrogance and the extremism in his mind. The roughness and the rudeness. That is the source of the sect of Al-Khawarij(الخوارج). Now, these same people are the ones who killed Uthman(عثمان). They're the same people; they didn't have the name Khawarij (خوارج) yet, but they're the ones who killed Uthman(عثمان). And they're the ones who caused the fight between Ali(علي) and Zubair(زبير) and Talha(طلحة). And they are the ones who are forcing the war between Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and Muawiyah(معاويه). And when they saw peace; they broke off. When they saw bloodshed; they participated and joined, when they saw blood. But when they saw peace among the Muslims; they didn't like it. And they wanted bloodshed to continue. And they broke off. Now, how do we know that these people, who broke off of the army of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) are the ones whom Rasool Allah ﷺ was talking about that, they would leave the religion? Rasool Allah ﷺ; he gave us a sign. And it's in this Hadith(حديث) narrated by Al-Bukhari(اَلْبُخَارِيْ). Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(أبو سعید الخدری) says, that Rasool Allah ﷺ describe, that one of them would be a dark man. One of his arms is like a breast of a woman. Meaning, there's no bone in his arm. It looks like a breast of a woman. Abu Saeed(أبو سعید الخدری) said; I was one of the ones who were fighting on the side of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) against Al-Khawarij(الخوارج). Because Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) went to them; he went to Al-Khawarij(الخوارج), and try to convince them. They refused. They said; You have betrayed the order of Allah. Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) said; then, I would give you three things. I would not prevent you from praying in our society; you can pray with us if you want to. And I will give you your share of Al-Fayy(..); the booties of war and the money of Muslim ummah(امة). When it is split among the Muslims; I will give you your share. Look at the forgiveness of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب). I will not forget you in your share; you will get your share. And number three; I will leave you alone, as long as you leave the Muslims alone. But they didn't leave the Muslims alone. The son of Khabbaab bin Arat( خباب بن أرت); the Sahabi(صحابي) of Rasool Allah ﷺ; his son and his wife were travelling in Iraq. Al-Khawarij(الخوارج); they stopped him. They had checkpoints. They stopped him. And they said; who are you?  He identified himself as the son of the Sahabi(صحابي); the companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ; Khabbaab bin Arat( خباب بن أرت). They asked him; whose side are you with. Are you with us or against us. He said; I'm not against you, but I'm with the truth. They killed him. His wife was pregnant; they opened up her stomach, and they pulled out the fetus, and they killed her. After that, Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) started war. That was the beginning of war between Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) and then. Because the deal was that, as long as you leave the Muslims alone; I'm going to leave you alone. But after that, that execution of the son of Sahabi(صحابي) of Rasool Allah ﷺ, and the brutal way of killing his wife; Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب)   wage war against them. In the Battle of Nahrwan(نہروان); Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) defeated them. And he killed many of them. Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(ابو سعيد الخذرى) said; I was one of the soldiers of Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب). Abu Saeed Al-Khudri(ابو سعيد الخذرى); the companion of Rasool Allah ﷺ; was narrated this Hadith(حديث). He said; Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) told us, to go and search for this man, whom Rasool Allah ﷺ described. He said; I went, and I saw him with my own eyes. And he had the exact descriptions of Rasool Allah ﷺ and he was laying with the dead. And that is a sign that Rasool Allah ﷺ was talking about these particular people. And Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) says about them that, there's a great reward for the one who kills them. And Rasool Allah ﷺ said; If I live until that time, I would kill them, like the people of Aad(عاد) were killed. Mean; complete elimination. Because the people of Aad(عاد) were eliminated . Rasool Allah ﷺ said; I would kill them, like the people of Aad(عاد) were eliminated. Why? Because, such a mentality; there's no way you could deal with, except through elimination; complete elimination. There's no way you could deal, with this extremism and thought, by reason; you cannot reason with them. These are people who are bloodthirsty. They want bloodshed. They're not going to settle for peace. How can you deal with them. Rasool Allah ﷺ said; therefore, there is a great reward in getting rid of them. Because if you leave them alone; they're not going to leave you alone, and they're going to cause Fitnah(فِتْنَه) in the ummah(امۃ). Therefore, the only way to deal with them is by elimination of their Fitnah(فِتْنَه). And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)! They have caused the Muslim ummah(امۃ); so much problem and so much Fitnah(فِتْنَه), because of them. I mean; some of the biggest Fitan(فتن), that happened in ummah(امة) was caused by Al-Khawarij(الخوارج). And it's a contradiction, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله)! The Muhadditheen(محدّثين) say, the scholar of Hadith(حديث) say; that we have never found anyone of the Khawarij(خوارج), who have ever lied on Rasool Allah ﷺ. They never fabricated Ahadith(احاديث). You find many of Ahl-e-Sunnat(اهل سنت); they fabricated Ahadith(احاديث); lies. But with the Khawarij(خوارج); they never lie. They're very sincere and truthful, but their minds are very stubborn. And they don't mind killing; they don't mind killing. Now, the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of Khawarij(خوارج) is not something that was temporary to that era. Rasool Allah ﷺ says that, their Fitnah(فِتْنَه) will continue. Whenever one generation of them leaves; another generation will come up again, until the time of the Ad-Dajjal(الدّجال). Rasool Allah ﷺ says; that their Fitnah(فِتْنَه) will continue. Whenever one generation of them leaves; what does that mean? Rasool Allah ﷺ did not say, it's a linear continuation. Rasool Allah ﷺ said; One generation would leave, and then another generation will come up .why? they cannot continue. Because they end up fighting among themselves. And they destroy themselves. And they kill each other out. Or they are killed by outside forces. But extremism then comes up in the minds of different people, and a new generation comes up. And then, they fight and they cause bloodshed, until they are eliminated. And then, they come out in another place. So it's not a linear continuation, where the one generation is teaching the next. Because, they cannot agree with each other. They end up fighting each other. They have a saying in Yemen that; he did not find anybody to disagree with; he disagreed with his own feet. You don't find anybody in front of you to disagree with; you under disagreeing with your own self. That's the mentality that they have. They have to make trouble. They have to fight to someone. And that’s why, Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

One generation would be followed by another.

This Hadith(حديث) is by Ibn Majah(ابن ماجه), Abdullah bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) says; I heard Rasool Allah ﷺ say, Whenever one generation of them comes out; it will be amputated, and then another generation will come out and it will be amputated. Abdullah bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) said; Rasool Allah ﷺ repeated it more than 20 times. And then in the end, he said; until Dajjal(دجال) will come out. So when generation will come out; it will be amputated. Either outside forces will amputate them, or they will amputate each other. And then another generation will come out, and will be amputated and so on and so forth. And Abdullah bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) used to consider them the most evil of people.

Abdullah bin Umar(عبدالله بن عمر) says, that they are the worst of people. Because, they took the Ayaat(آيات) referring to the non believers, and they applied them on the believers. They made Takfeer(تكفير) of the people. They accuse the Muslims of disbelief. They took the Ayaat(آيات) of Qur'an, which were describing the non believers, and they applied it on the Muslims. They're very easy in accusing people of disbelief. That is their major characteristic, is that it's very simple for them to accuse someone, or the Muslims of disbelief and Kuffr(كفر). The next Fitnah(فِتْنَه) is the death of Al-Hussain Ibn Ali Ibn Abi Talibرضي الله عنه . Rasool Allah ﷺ was once presented with red dirt. Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل عليه السلام) presented Rasool Allah ﷺ with red dirt; clay. And Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) told Rasool Allah ﷺ that your son; your grandson, Hussain(حسين) will be killed. And this is the dirt of the area, he will be killed in. He gave him a little bit of that dirt. Al-Hussain Ibn Ali Ibn Abi Talib(الحسين ابن علي ابن ابي طالب) was killed in; Karbala(كربلا). Al-Hussain Ibn Ali Ibn Abi Talib(الحسين ابن علي ابن ابي طالب), when his father was killed; he was given Baiyah(بَيْعة). And Hassan…... Al-Hassan(الحسن) was for six months. And then he gave it up. And then after that, Al-Hussain(الحسين); Al-Hussain Ibn Ali(الحسين ابن على), and some tribes of Iraq who promised him support. And a large group of Ahl al-Bayt(اهل البيت); relatives; his relatives from the household of Rasool Allah ﷺ. They fought with the army of bani Omayyah(بنى اميّه). And these tribes, who was promised them support; they betrayed them. In the end it was Al-Hussain Ibn Ali(الحسين ابن على) and his relatives from Ahl al-Bayt(اهل البيت). And they fought until the last person. And they were all killed in the end. And it was a big bloodshed of the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ. And this is a dark point in the history of the ummah(امة), that the ummah(امة) would do this to the family of Rasool Allah ﷺ. And that is obviously one of the biggest Fitan(فتن) that happened. It happened in the time of Yazeed bin Muawiyah(يزيد بن معاويه). Also Yazeed(يزيد); he committed another massacre in Madinah(مَدِينَه).

Where he attacked Madinah(مَدِينَه), and he committed bloodshed for days, and he killed many of the descendants of Al-Ansaar رضي الله عنهم, and from Al-Ansaar(ألأنْصَار). And Rasool Allah ﷺ said that, he saw that the rain of trials, of trouble was falling on the houses of Madinah(مَدِينَه). And this was a bloodshed that happened in Madinah(مَدِينَه). Most of these massacres bloodshed happens in the time of Yazeed bin Muawiyah(يزيد بن معاويه) in the time of his Khilafah(خِلَافَه). Sign number seven is the false prophets. Rasool Allah ﷺ says;

Rasool Allah ﷺ says; that the Day of Judgment will not occur until 30 false prophets arise; every one of them is claiming that he is a messenger. If we would sum up all of the people, who claim to be prophets in this Ummah(امة); we would find that they are more than 30. In the 1400 years have passed; they are more than 30. But Rasool Allah ﷺ in this Hadith(حديث) is talking about, and this Tafseer(تفسير) was also given by Shurrah-ul-Hadith(شرّاح الحديث); the explainers of the Hadith(حديث). They say, this is talking about the false prophets, who end up having a sizable following and become famous and well known. But the crazy people here and there, who every day, you find somebody, some of them claiming to be prophets; this is not talking about them. This is talking about people who had the sizable following, and they became famous, and they formed sect, or they had a group following them. Among the most famous of these are two false prophets, who claim to be prophets in the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ. And these two were Musaylima Al-Kadhab(مسيلمه الكذّاب) in Al-Yamama Bani Hanifah(اليمامه بنى حنيفه), and Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(الاسود الانسى) in Sana’a, Yemen. These two are the first. And this happened was the end of the life of Rasool Allah ﷺ. Musaylima Al-Kadhab(مسيلمه الكذّاب) was from the Bedouins of Banu Hanifah(بنو حنيفه). This is a big tribe, who live in the area of Al-Yamama(اليمامه) in Arabia, and he was playing on the tribalism tone. Rasool Allah ﷺ is from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), and from Banu Hanifah(بنو حنيفه), they are from Al-Hazar(الحضر), they are from Ahl al Madhar(اهل المضر). They are from the urban from the city dwellers; they are the rural people. So he was playing on those nationalism issues. And you find that these false prophets; they always try to use deceptive ways to attract the people. This man Musaylima Al-Kadhab(مسيلمه الكذّاب), he used this. Because he knew that the hearts of the people; they still had nationalism in their hearts. So he played on that. And one of his big followers, actually his right hand supporter. He used to say clearly;

He used to say that, the liars of Bani Hanifah(بنى حنيفه) is better than the truthful of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ). But he's from my people, is better than the true man Muhammadﷺ, who's from Quraish(قُرَيْشْ). Many of them knew that he's lying. Because his Qur'an was funny. And Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! This is a miracle that you would find people, who are intelligent and are very good in poems and poetry. But whenever they try to imitate Qur'an; the product is miserable and funny. When they try to imitate Qur'an, Subhan Allah(سُبْحان الله)! They come up with something that is unbelievable. Abu ul Ala' Al-Muarri(ابو العلاء المعري); he was one of the most well known and famous Arab poets. He was a blind man. Allahسُبحانه وتعالى Has given him such an ability and eloquence in language. He is one of the most famous poets in the history of the Arabic language. They said that, for a while, he sat down to produce a Qur'an. He had this ego issue. He was a very proud person. He had such an ego and he was an arrogant personality. He thought that, he could compete with the word of Allah سبحانہ تعالی. So he sat down in his home for a long time; trying to produce a Qur'an. After a while, they saw that, he was ignoring the project. The people were asking; Where's the Qur'an that you promised? He said; Forget about it, I burned it, I couldn't do it. Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب); even though his Qur'an was miserable, and funny; he had such a huge following. Hundreds of 1000s of people followed him. Huge following. And it was a big Fitnah(فِتْنَه). And his Fitnah(فِتْنَه) was not extinguished until the time of Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه. And that was one of the worst battles that the Muslims have to confront. Many, many of the Muslims died in that battle to the extent that, 10s of Haffaz(حفّاظ) were being killed. 10s of Haffaz(حفّاظ) who were memorizes Qur'an were be massacred and killed. And that's how the process of collecting Qur'an, gathering Qur'an started. And that's when Abu Bakr As-Siddique(أبوبكرالصديق); he started with the project of combining Qur'an and bringing Qur'an. The Mushaf(مصحف) together. And then the project was completed in time of Uthman(عثمان). And the famous battle of Al-Hadeeqah(الحديقة), that is when Musailimah Al-Kazzab(مسيلمة ألكذاب) was eventually killed. Rasool Allah ﷺ saw a dream, where he was wearing two bracelets of gold.

I was concerned. And then, Allah told me to blow on them; So I blew on them and they flew away. They asked Rasool Allah ﷺ; What is the Tab'eer(تعبير), what is the interpretation of that dream? He said; I interpreted the two liars, who will come up in my Ummah(امة). And this talking about Musaylimah(مسيلمة) and Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(الاسود الانسى). So Musaylimah(مسيلمة) was killed. He got married to a woman named Sajah(سجاح). Who claimed to be a prophet too. This woman; she claimed to be a prophet. She had a certain following, Musaylimah(مسيلمة) had a certain following; they decided for political reasons to marry, and to come together. It was a political marriage. And they married each other. When Musaylimah(مسيلمة) was killed; she found out that this profit-hood thing is not giving her any advances. So she forget about it, and she became a Muslim again. Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(الاسود الانسى) he was killed by a man named Feroz(فيروز) in Yemen. They assassinated him, actually they went into his palace, and they assassinated him, and that was the end of Al-Aswad Al-Ansi(الاسود الانسى). And then we have Tulayhah Al-Asdi(طليحه الاسدى). Tulayhah Al-Asdi(طليحه الاسدى) also claimed to be a prophet, but he gave up this claim and he became a Muslim. And they say,

His Islam was fine after that. This is Tulayhah alUsdi. And Allah-u-Aalam(اللَّهُ أَعْلمَ)! Ho Alam(الله أعلم)! it was Tulayhah(طليحه) or Musaylimah(مسيلمة),one of them, whenever they would asking to read Qur'an; he would be talking about the Ayaat(آيات) that are describing food. Too much description of food. So then they told him;

They told him; we don't know if the angel is revealing to your heart or revealing to your stomach. All of the Ayaat(آيات) are talking about food. They told him, we don't know where the angel is speaking to. Maybe he is speaking to your stomach. And then, Mukhtar Ibn Obaid Athaqafi(المختار ابن عبيد الثقفي); he also acclaimed to be a prophet. And, in the modern times we have Mirza Ghulam Ahmad(مرزا غلام اَحْمَدْ), who claim to be a prophet. Mirza Ghulam Ahmad(مرزا غلام اَحْمَدْ); he is the founder of Al-Qadiyaniya(القاديانيه). He claimed to be a prophet, and he counts as one of the 30, because he has a sizable following. It's a serious movement, he has a quite a big following and it's a big Fitnah(فِتْنَه). It's a big Fitnah(فِتْنَه); the Fitnah(فِتْنَه) of Al-Qadiyaniya(القاديانيه). And it is Kuffr(كفر), not only by the standards of Shariah(شريعة) but also handled politically in Pakistan. There has been a law that states that it is not a form of Islam, officially.
